export const SKILL_FILES: Record<string, string> = {
  "SKILL.md": "---\nname: hedgesync\ndescription: Read, edit and collaborate live in HedgeDoc notes (collaborative Markdown, also known as CodiMD) with the hedgesync CLI or its MCP server. Use when the user shares a HedgeDoc note URL (e.g. https://md.example.com/abc123), asks to read, update, summarize, search or create HedgeDoc notes, or wants an agent to work in a note alongside people, e.g. answering requests written into it.\nlicense: MIT\ncompatibility: Needs the hedgesync CLI (npm install -g hedgesync, or a release binary) and network access to the HedgeDoc server.\nmetadata:\n  homepage: https://github.com/tionis/hedgesync\n---\n\n# HedgeDoc notes with hedgesync\n\nHedgeDoc notes are Markdown documents that several people edit at the same\ntime. hedgesync edits them through the same realtime connection a browser\nuses: your edit merges with what people are typing right now and shows up in\ntheir editors at once. So **edit small and targeted**, never download, change\nand upload the whole note while others work in it.\n\n## MCP tools or CLI?\n\nIf tools such as `read_note`, `edit_note` and `wait_for_change` are available\n(the hedgesync MCP server), use them: they keep a live session open, show your\ncursor to others and return structured results. Otherwise use the CLI below.\nBoth use the same login.\n\n## Before you start\n\n```sh\nhedgesync me https://md.example.com      # who you are signed in as there\n```\n\nIf that says you are not signed in, notes that anyone may edit still work as a\nguest. For everything else, ask the user to sign in once (it opens nothing, it\nreuses their browser session; don't run it for them unasked):\n\n```sh\nhedgesync login https://md.example.com --from-browser firefox --save   # or chrome, ...\n```\n\n## Reading\n\n```sh\nhedgesync get <url>                 # the note's current text (live, including unsaved typing)\nhedgesync info <url>                # title, permission, who is in it now\nhedgesync list <server-url>         # notes in the user's history (-s <text> to filter, --json)\nhedgesync search <server-url> <pattern> [-i]   # lines matching, across the user's notes\n```\n\n## Editing (live)\n\n```sh\nhedgesync replace <url> 'exact old text' 'new text'   # first occurrence; --all for every one\nhedgesync append <url> 'text'                         # at the end (also: -f file, or stdin)\nhedgesync prepend <url> 'text'\nhedgesync set <url> -f note.md                        # whole note, applied as a minimal diff\nhedgesync create <server-url> -f note.md              # a new note; prints its URL\n```\n\n- Read the note right before changing it, and copy `old text` exactly from it.\n- If `replace` finds nothing, someone changed that text meanwhile: read again.\n- Use `set` only for notes nobody else is editing, or for full rewrites the\n  user asked for; it overwrites concurrent typing in the changed parts.\n- Text with quotes, `$` or newlines: pass it on stdin or with `-f`, e.g.\n  `printf '%s\\n' '- [ ] item' | hedgesync append <url>`.\n- Markdown conventions in HedgeDoc: the first `# Heading` is the title; YAML\n  front matter (`---`) holds `title`, `tags`, `type: slide`. Change those with\n  `hedgesync meta <url>` (see `hedgesync help meta`).\n\n## Working with people in a note\n\nTo act on requests people write into a note (e.g. lines mentioning\n`@agent`), prefer the MCP tool `wait_for_change` with `until: \"@agent\"`: it\nreturns what changed and who changed it, then you act and wait again. Without\nMCP, `hedgesync watch <url> --ndjson` streams changes, but it never exits on\nits own; run it in the background or with a timeout. For a ready-made bot that\nanswers mentions with an LLM, see `hedgesync help assistant`.\n\nWhen you answer in a note, write below the request and mark it handled (e.g.\nreplace `@agent` with `✓`), so it is not picked up twice.\n\n## Setting up the MCP server\n\nIf the user wants the MCP tools, see [references/mcp.md](references/mcp.md):\n`claude mcp add hedgesync -- hedgesync mcp --server https://md.example.com`\nfor Claude Code, and setups for other agents, read-only and single-note modes,\nand HTTP with OAuth.\n\n## More\n\n`hedgesync help` lists every command; `hedgesync help <command>` explains\none. [references/cli.md](references/cli.md) covers the less common ones\n(permissions, revisions, uploads, exports, macros, mirroring).\n",
  "references/cli.md": "# Less common hedgesync commands\n\nAll take a note URL unless noted; `hedgesync help <command>` has the details\nand `--json` gives machine-readable output for most.\n\n| Task | Command |\n|---|---|\n| Change a line (0-based) | `hedgesync line <url> 3 'new text'` |\n| Regex replace | `hedgesync replace <url> '- \\[ \\]' '- [x]' --regex --all` |\n| Insert at a character offset | `hedgesync insert <url> 120 'text'` |\n| Note settings (title, tags, type, ...) | `hedgesync meta <url>`, `hedgesync meta <url> tags a b`, `--add-tag x` |\n| Who may view/edit | `hedgesync permission <url>`, `hedgesync permission <url> limited` |\n| Who wrote what | `hedgesync authors <url>` |\n| Who is online | `hedgesync users <url>` |\n| Revisions | `hedgesync revisions <url>` (list), `<url> <rev>` (content), `<url> <rev> --diff`, `<url> <rev> --restore` |\n| Download without a live session | `hedgesync download <url>` |\n| Upload an image, get Markdown | `hedgesync upload <server-url> shot.png` |\n| Published / slide URL | `hedgesync publish <url>` |\n| Export all notes (zip) | `hedgesync export <server-url> -o notes.zip` |\n| History | `hedgesync history <server-url>`, `pin`, `unpin`, `history-delete` |\n| Keep a local file and a note in sync | `hedgesync share file.md <server-url>` (new note) or `share file.md <note-url>` |\n| Two notes in sync | `hedgesync mirror <url-a> <url-b>` |\n| Pandoc transform, heading levels | `hedgesync transform <url> --promote`, `--to <format>` |\n| Expand text macros as people type | `hedgesync macro <url> --built-in --watch` |\n| Answer @mentions with an LLM | `hedgesync assistant <url> --agent claude` |\n| Append to notes from webhooks | `hedgesync serve --note name=<url>` |\n| Delete a note (owner only, irreversible) | `hedgesync delete <url>` |\n\nAsk before anything irreversible or visible to others beyond the note at\nhand: `delete`, `permission`, `revisions --restore`, and `set` on a note\npeople are working in.\n\nPermission values: `freely` (anyone edits), `editable` (anyone views, signed-in\nusers edit), `limited` (signed-in users only), `locked`, `protected`, `private`\n(see `hedgesync help permission`).\n\nLogins: `hedgesync login <server> --from-browser <browser> --save` reuses a\nbrowser session; `hedgesync sessions` lists saved ones; `HEDGEDOC_COOKIE`\noverrides them.\n",
  "references/mcp.md": "# The hedgesync MCP server\n\n`hedgesync mcp` serves HedgeDoc notes over the Model Context Protocol. It\nspeaks the current revision (2026-07-28) and the 2025 ones.\n\n## Tools\n\n| Group | Tool | What it does |\n|---|---|---|\n| read | `list_notes` | Notes in the user's history (title, URL, tags) |\n| read | `search_notes` | Lines matching a pattern, across those notes |\n| read | `read_note` | Live text with line numbers; `section` or `lines` for part of a long note |\n| read | `wait_for_change` | Waits until people change the note (optionally until some text appears), returns a diff and who did it |\n| edit | `edit_note` | Replace exact text (unique, or `replace_all`) |\n| edit | `edit_section` | Replace, append to or prepend to the section under a heading; `create: true` adds it |\n| edit | `append_to_note` | Add text at the end |\n| edit | `write_note` | Replace the whole note; refused if it changed since you read it |\n| create | `create_note` | New note, returns its URL |\n\nNotes are also resources: the note URL is the resource URI, and subscribers\nare told when the note changes. The prompt `work_in_note` sets an agent up to\ntake requests written into a note.\n\n## Registering it\n\nClaude Code:\n\n```sh\nclaude mcp add hedgesync -- hedgesync mcp --server https://md.example.com\n```\n\nCodex (`~/.codex/config.toml`):\n\n```toml\n[mcp_servers.hedgesync]\ncommand = \"hedgesync\"\nargs = [\"mcp\", \"--server\", \"https://md.example.com\"]\n```\n\nCursor (`.cursor/mcp.json`), Gemini CLI (`~/.gemini/settings.json`) and most\nothers:\n\n```json\n{ \"mcpServers\": { \"hedgesync\": { \"command\": \"hedgesync\", \"args\": [\"mcp\", \"--server\", \"https://md.example.com\"] } } }\n```\n\nVS Code (`.vscode/mcp.json`):\n\n```json\n{ \"servers\": { \"hedgesync\": { \"type\": \"stdio\", \"command\": \"hedgesync\", \"args\": [\"mcp\", \"--server\", \"https://md.example.com\"] } } }\n```\n\n`hedgesync agent config <client>` prints these with the right paths.\n\n## Limiting what an agent can do\n\n```sh\nhedgesync mcp --read-only                          # only the read tools\nhedgesync mcp --tools read,edit                    # tool groups: read, edit, create\nhedgesync mcp --note https://md.example.com/plan   # only this note (repeatable)\n```\n\n## Over HTTP\n\n```sh\nhedgesync mcp --http 8788                                   # loopback only, no sign-in\nhedgesync mcp --http 0.0.0.0:8788 --token \"$SECRET\"         # bearer token\nhedgesync mcp --http 8788 --public-url https://mcp.example.com --owner https://you.example.com\n```\n\nWith `--owner`, the server is an OAuth 2.1 authorization server: clients\nregister themselves, the owner approves them in a browser and signs in with\nIndieAuth (their website names their IndieAuth server), and token scopes\n(`read`, `edit`, `create`) pick the tools. Connect with, e.g.,\n`claude mcp add --transport http hedgedoc https://mcp.example.com/mcp`.\n\nWhoever gets in works as the HedgeDoc login of the machine running the server.\n",
};
